//! Auxiliary `ext_params` that a composite functional overrides.
//!
//! GENERATED by `verify/tests/gen_aux_overrides.rs` from libxc 7.0.0
//! itself -- do not hand-edit. Regenerate with:
//!
//! ```text
//! LIBXC_RS_WRITE_AUX_OVERRIDES=1 cargo test --release \
//!     --manifest-path verify/Cargo.toml --test gen_aux_overrides -- --nocapture
//! ```
//!
//! When libxc builds a composite with `xc_mix_init`, the parent's init
//! and setter may override its auxiliaries' parameters: `lc_blyp` hands
//! its `_omega` down to `gga_x_ityh`, `gga_x_sogga` overrides PBE's
//! `_kappa` and `_mu`, HSE06 pins one leg's `_omega` to zero. Without
//! this table each auxiliary ran on its own defaults, which for 47 of
//! the 125 composite GGAs is a different functional entirely.
//!
//! Each row is read straight out of libxc's `xc_func_type` after
//! `xc_func_init` and compared against that auxiliary's own declared
//! default, so the values are libxc's own answer rather than a
//! transcription of its C.
//!
//! **Snapshot at the parent's default ext_params.** Changing a parent
//! parameter that feeds an auxiliary leaves this stale unless
//! `composite_setters` or `PROPAGATION_RULES` also describes the
//! relationship -- which is why those tables still exist.
#![allow(clippy::all)]

